              "jcr:created": "Thu Mar 13 2025 18:21:48 GMT+0000",
              "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
              "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">VertaPlex<sup>®</sup> HV bone cement</span></span></span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">VertaPlex HV bone cement is used for treating vertebral compression fractures.<sup><a href=\"#references\">2</a></sup> It reaches a thick viscosity as soon as it's mixed and maintains viscosity for an average of 18 minutes.<sup><a href=\"#references\">3</a></sup></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">VertaPlex HV cement was introduced in 2009 to address specific viscosity and working time preferences for physicians. In 2015, VertaPlex HV became the first polymethylmethacrylate (PMMA) cement in the U.S. to receive 510(k) clearance for the fixation of pathological fractures of the sacral vertebral body or ala using sacral vertebroplasty or sacroplasty.<sup><a href=\"#references\">4</a></sup></span></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Feb 02 2026 14:14:29 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "backgroundColor": "rgb(237,238,236)",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            },
            "accordion_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 12 2025 14:22:25 GMT+0000",
