  "disclaimer": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
    "disclaimer-type": "text",
    "disclaimer": "<ol>\r\n<li>Stryker data on file.</li>\r\n<li>Stryker Corporation. VertaPlex HV Radiopaque Bone Cement Instructions for Use 0406-622-715 Rev-AD. Retrieved on July 30, 2025 from <a href=\"https://labeling.stryker.com/hcp/XHR/US/pthxr?keycode=07613252254430\">https://labeling.stryker.com/hcp/XHR/US/pthxr?keycode=07613252254430</a></li>\r\n<li>Independent lab results from Fluid Dynamics Inc commissioned by Stryker (July 2009). Testing conducted at 20-21 ˚C (68-70 ˚F).</li>\r\n<li>U.S. Food and Drug Administration. (2020). 510(k) Premarket Notification: K192818 - OptaBlate RF Ablation Probe. Retrieved on July 30, 2025 from <a href=\"https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=k192818\">https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cdrh/cfdocs/cfpmn/pmn.cfm?ID=k192818</a></li>\r\n<li>Davies J et al. The effect of centrifuging bone cement. J Bone Joint Surg Br. 1989; 71(1):39-42.</li>\r\n<li>Hansen D and Jensen J. Mixing does not improve mechanical properties of all bone cements. Manual and centrifugation-vacuum mixing compared for 10 cement brands. Acta Orthop Scand 1992; 63(1): 13-18.</li>\r\n<li>Holm N. The relaxation of some acrylic bone cements. Acta Orthop Scand. 1980; 51(5):727-31.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Aug 08 2025 17:24:28 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/structure/disclaimer",
    "textIsRich": "true"
  },
  "image": {
